{
  "id": "T18_63_a_normalization_naming_an_interpretation_the_reference_lacks_is_refused",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "10.2.9",
    "7.3.8",
    "10.3",
    "12.17",
    "8.1.2",
    "10.2.2",
    "8.3.1"
  ],
  "description": "A normalization naming an interpretation the reference does not have, an application interpretation or a version of a fixture interpretation that the reference does not provide, fails 10.2.9 and leaves the store unchanged: its triple then takes a normalization the reference has, and a statement that references the refused normalization fails 10.2.2. A replace correction whose corrected values would make a normalization name such an interpretation fails 10.2.9 and records nothing. After a retire_interpretation step removes the fixture set interpretation, an identical write of a normalization, and of a replace correction, recorded while the reference had it is a replay, while a new normalization naming it, or a correction that would make a normalization name it, fails 10.2.9. A normalization naming literal comparison is accepted.",
  "note": "10.2.9: \"a normalization whose `@interpretation` names an interpretation that the implementation does not have (7.3.8), or a `replace` correction whose `@corrected` values are such a normalization (8.3.1). An identical write of one already recorded is a replay (8.1.2)\". 7.3.8: \"An implementation records a normalization only when it has the interpretation the normalization names, so that it can perform the maintenance the normalization requires (*Recording*, below): one naming an interpretation it does not have is rejected (10.2.9).\" 12.17: writing such a normalization \"is rejected (10.2.9), and so is writing any record that references it, such as an end act citing it, because the reference does not resolve (10.2.2).\" README section 5, Interpretations: the reference provides each fixture interpretation \"at version `\\\"1\\\"`\", and \"Any other name is unavailable, and so is a fixture interpretation after a `retire_interpretation` step that names it\"; 7.3.8: \"Two interpretations are the same when they have the same name and version.\" README section 6, item 8. No unit lies in the zones, so the accepted writes record nothing.",
